    {
      "id": 301,
      "slug": "why-we-run-a-bug-hunt",
      "title": "Why the club runs its own bug hunt",
      "authorId": 1,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-15",
      "tags": [
        "club",
        "security"
      ],
      "readMinutes": 6,
      "excerpt": "Reading code carefully is a skill you cannot outsource. Here is how we train it.",
      "body": "We noticed something during last year review week. Everyone could generate code. Almost nobody could read it.\n\nSo we built a portal, planted defects in it on purpose, and asked members to hunt. The rules are simple: find it, prove it, document it.\n\nThe hunt is not about tooling. It is about attention.",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "authorId": 6,
          "body": "Looking forward to the kickoff briefing!",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-15T18:20:00+05:30"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "authorId": 2,
          "body": "Noted, we will confirm at the kickoff briefing.",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-15T19:02:00+05:30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 302,
      "slug": "self-hosting-on-a-pi",
      "title": "Self hosting the club stack on one Raspberry Pi",
      "authorId": 4,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-28",
      "tags": [
        "selfhost",
        "infra"
      ],
      "readMinutes": 9,
      "excerpt": "Caddy, three containers and a fan that is far too loud.",
      "body": "The Pi runs attendly, pi-signage and a Gitea instance. Total idle RAM is under 700MB.\n\nCaddy handles TLS. Backups are a nightly rsync to a spare SSD taped to the wall.",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 3,
          "authorId": 8,
          "body": "Add Prometheus node_exporter, I can share the compose file.",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-29T09:14:00+05:30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 304,
      "slug": "first-pr-guide",
      "title": "Your first pull request, start to merge",
      "authorId": 3,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-19",
      "tags": [
        "beginner",
        "git"
      ],
      "readMinutes": 5,
      "excerpt": "Fork, branch, commit, push, open, respond. Nothing else.",
      "body": "Most first PRs fail on the commit message, not the code.\n\nWrite what changed and why. Reviewers read the why first.",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 4,
          "authorId": 9,
          "body": "This got my FreeCAD patch merged, thanks.",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-20T11:40:00+05:30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 305,
      "slug": "reading-cve-reports",
      "title": "How to read a CVE report without panicking",
      "authorId": 2,
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-30",
      "tags": [
        "security"
      ],
      "readMinutes": 8,
      "excerpt": "Severity is context. A 9.8 you cannot reach is less urgent than a 5.3 on your login page.",
      "body": "Start with the attack vector, not the score. Ask who can reach the code path and what they need to already have.\n\nThen check whether your deployment even enables the feature.",
      "comments": []
    },
